 the <b>spring sowbread</b>, is a species of flowering plant of the family Primulaceae, native to southern Europe and some Mediterranean islands. It is the most widespread of a group of cyclamens (genus <i>Cyclamen</i> subgenus <i>Psilanthum</i>) with wide, heart-shaped leaves, often coarsely toothed or lobed, and late spring-blooming flowers with long, slender petals.", "vision": true}}